A||||1||saleenfiero||What is the proper process for spray bombing?||||1||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||06-07-2001||03:51 PM||||I want to repaint my wing myself, but what is the proper tehcnique and way to do it?  How much to sand and which grits before painting, how and what to sand with after paint is applied?  I'm not going for total perfection here, just long enough to look okay until I paint the car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-07-2001||06:31 PM||||if the clears peeling, turning white, youll have to sand it off first. use something coarser, like #260-360 then finist up with #400-600. if you just need to scuff it up skip the first one. Spray a coat of laquer primer (sandable one) to seal it, then sand lightly.  then just spray your color in long strokes well overlapped, stopping spray at end of each pass. Depending on color, it will take 2-4 coats, if you use basecoat colors, youll have to finish with coats of clear over that.||||reg||1
